adjudication.rationale:
In the new plural-IDs branch of `_hydrateEmbedded` (matching `/_id(s?)$/`), it does:

```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(id => self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root));
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
```

`Array.prototype.map` always returns an Array (so `hydrated || []` is effectively dead/unreachable unless `obj[k]` isn’t an array—in which case it would throw before this line). More importantly, `_lookupSubType` can return a falsy value (the singular case explicitly guards `if (hydrated) { ... }`), but the plural case does not, so the assigned array can contain `undefined`/null entries for IDs that can’t be hydrated, changing behavior vs. the singular path and potentially breaking consumers expecting an array of records.
